      "title": "TCP: Use RFC 6994 for experimental options",
      "message": "TCP: Use RFC 6994 for experimental options\n\nModernize the handling of experimental TCP options based on\nRFC 6994. In particular use ExID instead of magic (which\nin the context of RFC 6994 are the last two bytes of a\n32-bit ExID) and add a desciption of ExID based on the\ncurrent state of the IANA registry.\n",
      "author_name": "Michael Tuexen",
      "author_email": "tuexen@wireshark.org",
      "authored_date": "2022-08-17T22:13:48.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "A Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2022-08-17T21:33:31.000+00:00",
